# Rust
/tabular-center-rust/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Kotlin / Gradle
#
# Unanchored, because Gradle writes a `.gradle/` beside every build file and
# this repository now has four: tabular-center-kotlin/ksp, tabular-center-kotlin/ksp/compile-fail,
# tabular-center-kotlin/examples/06-generated, and whatever comes next. The anchored patterns
# below reached only the first level, so `tabular-center-kotlin/ksp/.gradle/executionHistory`
# was committed -- caches, locks and machine-specific paths in git history.
#
# Already-tracked copies are not removed by a pattern. That takes
#
#   git rm -r --cached tabular-center-kotlin/ksp/.gradle tabular-center-kotlin/ksp/compile-fail/.gradle
#
# once, and then they stay out.
.gradle/
/tabular-center-kotlin/**/build/

/tabular-center-kotlin/.gradle/
/tabular-center-kotlin/build/
/tabular-center-kotlin/codegen/emitted/
/tabular-center-kotlin/*/build/
/tabular-center-kotlin/.gradle-home/
# The dev shells anchor GRADLE_USER_HOME at tabular-center-kotlin/.gradle-home.
# Kept unanchored as well, for a shell entered before that change, which put
# it wherever `nix develop` was typed.
.gradle-home/
# Kotlin
#
# The module builds with `kotlinc` directly for now, which writes wherever it
# is told rather than into a build directory a build system would already
# ignore. 59 class files and a 4.7 MB jar reached a commit before this existed.
/tabular-center-kotlin/out/
/tabular-center-kotlin/testout/
/tabular-center-kotlin/testout.jar
/tabular-center-kotlin/build/
/tabular-center-kotlin/codegen/emitted/

# Swift
/tabular-center-swift/.build/
/tabular-center-swift/Package.resolved
/tabular-center-swift/*.xcodeproj
# The macro package is a SEPARATE SwiftPM package, so the anchored patterns
# above do not reach it.
/tabular-center-swift/macros/.build/

# `tabular-center-swift/macros/Package.resolved` is deliberately NOT ignored, unlike the one
# above it. The main package has no dependencies, so its resolved file pins
# nothing and committing it would be noise. This one pins swift-syntax to a
# revision, and `tabular-center-swift/tools/swift-lock` reads that revision to build the offline
# artifact set -- so it is the input to a lock rather than a build artifact.
# Nix
.direnv/
result
result-*
# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Examples build output
#
# Not just 07-compose: the anchored Kotlin patterns above stop at /kotlin/, so
# every Gradle example writes a build/ nothing was ignoring -- 06-generated
# included, which had simply never been built in a working tree before.
/tabular-center-kotlin/examples/*/build/
/tabular-center-rust/examples/target/
/tabular-center-fmt/target/
/tabular-center-rust/examples/05-iced/target/
/tabular-center-swift/examples/.build/
/tabular-center-swift/examples/Package.resolved

# Rendered locally by `nix run .#docs`. The published site is rendered by
# GitHub Pages from doc/ itself, so this directory is a preview artifact only.
/doc/_site/
.jekyll-cache/

# doc/ is generated by tools/docs AND committed: Pages serves it from the
# branch. `tools/verify docs` fails if it is stale. The old uncommitted
# location is still ignored so a leftover local copy stays out of commits.
/docs/

# The Pages site: build output of tools/docs, deployed by .github/workflows/pages.yml.
/doc/
